          "description": "<p>Crabrawler is a fantastic bulky attacker that checks dangerous threats such as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/growlithe-hisui/lc/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hisuian Growlithe</a> and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/toedscool/lc/\" hreflang=\"en\">Toedscool</a>, and can sweep teams with Bulk Up. Coverage moves such as Ice Punch, Thunder Punch, and Earthquake offer Crabrawler extreme flexibility in the threats it needs to cover. Ice Punch hits <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/foongus/lc/\" hreflang=\"en\">Foongus</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/wattrel/lc/\" hreflang=\"en\">Wattrel</a>, and Toedscool, while Thunder Punch hits <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/mareanie/lc/\" hreflang=\"en\">Mareanie</a>, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/wingull/lc/\" hreflang=\"en\">Wingull</a>, and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/quaxly/lc/\" hreflang=\"en\">Quaxly</a>; both options also hit <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/drifloon/lc/\" hreflang=\"en\">Drifloon</a> super effectively. Earthquake allows Crabrawler to hit Mareanie and <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/fuecoco/lc/\" hreflang=\"en\">Fuecoco</a> and is its strongest neutral option against <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/zorua-hisui/lc/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hisuian Zorua</a>. Tera Fire makes Crabrawler immune to burns, while Tera Electric makes Thunder Punch stronger against Water-types and gives it defensive utility against threats like <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/voltorb-hisui/lc/\" hreflang=\"en\">Hisuian Voltorb</a> and Wingull. Crabrawler hates dealing with opposing Ghost-types such as Hisuian Zorua, <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/greavard/lc/\" hreflang=\"en\">Greavard</a>, and Drifloon, as well as <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/gothita/lc/\" hreflang=\"en\">Gothita</a>. Hisuian Growlithe checks these threats and makes an excellent teammate for Crabrawler, as do Ghost-types such as Hisuian Zorua and Drifloon that benefit from the removal of opposing <a href=\"/dex/sv/pokemon/pawniard/lc/\" hreflang=\"en\">Pawniard</a>.</p>",
